        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the range of the height of students in the class?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$38\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "The smallest height is $144\\text{ cm}$ and the largest is $182\\text{ cm}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Range}&=182-144\\\\\\text{Range}&=38\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the median height of students in the class?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$161.5\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "There are 20 heights, so the median is the average of the 10th and 11th values, $161$ and $162$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=\\frac{161+162}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=161.5\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the interquartile range?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$22.5\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "Divide the ordered heights into two groups of 10. The lower quartile is the average of the 5th and 6th values overall; the upper quartile is the average of the 15th and 16th values overall.\n$$\\begin{align*}Q_1&=\\frac{151+152}{2}\\\\Q_1&=151.5\\text{ cm}\\\\Q_3&=\\frac{172+176}{2}\\\\Q_3&=174\\text{ cm}\\\\\\text{IQR}&=174-151.5\\\\\\text{IQR}&=22.5\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
